index bbe5f9ec7..537c87054 100644
--- a/packages/web/server/lib/gitea/DOCUMENTATION.md
+++ b/packages/web/server/lib/gitea/DOCUMENTATION.md
@@ -31,7 +31,8 @@ Target: Gitea 1.21 or newer, verified against live 1.21.11 and 1.27.3 (see *Veri
 - Labels are set as a whole set by name; names are turned into the repository's label ids (`PUT /issues/{n}/labels`). A name the repository does not have is a 422. Organization labels are not looked up.
 - Reviewers are set as a whole set by numeric user id, like GitLab's. Ids are turned into usernames through the collaborators and the current review requests, then the difference is sent as `POST` (add) and `DELETE` (remove) on `requested_reviewers`. The two calls are not atomic; reconciliation succeeds only when the current set matches. Gitea lists in `requested_reviewers` everyone with a standing review, not only open requests, and a `DELETE` for someone who already reviewed answers 204 and changes nothing. So before any write, a removal reads `/pulls/{n}/reviews` and refuses with `400 GITEA_REVIEWER_HAS_REVIEWED`, naming the logins, when someone to remove has a submitted review (`APPROVED`, `REQUEST_CHANGES` or `COMMENT`, not dismissed). 1.21 answers an empty set as `null`, read as empty.
 - `head.label` is the bare branch name even for a fork's branch, so `headLabel` is built as `owner:branch` from `head.repo`, the form the worktree flow reads an owner from.
-- Capabilities off: review threads (no reply or resolve API), uploads (attachments are served to a browser session), stacks, the reference picker.
+- The reference picker's per-repository lists stay list-backed (`referenceSearch`, `referenceDetail` and `listStatuses` off): the client reads them through `listIssues` and `listChangeRequests` and previews them through `getIssue`, `issueComments` and `changeRequestContext`. The one provider-owned read is the search across a folder's repositories (`references/across`, `referencesAcross`): Gitea has no search that names a set of repositories, so `references-across.js` reads the newest page of each folder's repository (`/pulls` for an unfiltered pull list, `/issues?type=pulls` for a filtered or merged one, `/repos/issues/search` for review requests) and merges them by activity. A pull request from the issue search carries no head or base, so only the items that land on the page are read as `/pulls/{n}` before they are mapped; one that moved away is dropped from the page, not failed. A page covers at most four pages per repository (200 items at the 50-item cap), and per-repository pages are cached for 30 s so paging does not read every repository again. A folder with no repository on the instance answers `no-repo`, a stale binding `invalid-context`, a signed-out account `disconnected`; the other folders still answer.
+- Capabilities off: review threads (no reply or resolve API), uploads (attachments are served to a browser session), stacks, discussions.
 
